From 3e2a4372acdb02dace97d8724cb97fe73177a48a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 04:08:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 068/104] demux: asf: leave the timeline alone on a seek

SeekPrepare() told the output to reset its pcr on every seek. The input
has already reset whatever the seek needs reset by the time it calls the
demuxer - the decoders, the clock reference and the buffering state - so
for an ordinary seek this said nothing new.

A repeat in place is the case where it is not redundant but wrong. There
the input deliberately does not flush: the audio the output still holds
is what covers the gap while the demuxer starts over, and the clock
reference is what carries the new pass onto the end of the old one. The
reset undid all of it, so every loop flushed the output, re-entered
buffering, waited for the whole cushion again and lost the tail the
output was still holding.

Say nothing and let the input's own reset stand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/asf/asf.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/asf/asf.c b/modules/demux/asf/asf.c
index 1862faa818..31d98855ea 100644
--- a/modules/demux/asf/asf.c
+++ b/modules/demux/asf/asf.c
@@ -424,8 +424,6 @@ static void SeekPrepare( demux_t *p_demux )
             tk->i_time = -1;
         }
     }
-
-    es_out_Control( p_demux->out, ES_OUT_RESET_PCR );
 }
 
